<title>USA: Tesoro not part of KCS/Tenneco litigation.</title>
<headline>Tesoro not part of KCS/Tenneco litigation.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tesoro Petroleum Co said Monday it holds no interest in South Texas producing properties operated by a subsidiary of KCS Energy Inc, which has been the subject of litigation between KCS and Tennessee Gas Pipeline Co.</p>
<p>Early Monday, KCS said a jury awarded the Tenneco Inc subsidiary $143 million.</p>
<p>Saying it was responding to numerous inquiries, Tesoro said its producing interests in the Bob West Field are operated by Coastal Corp and Sanchez-O'Brien Oil and Gas Corp.</p>
<p>Tenneco Energy spokesman Russell Johnson said no companies were involved in this litigation except the Tenneco pipeline and KCS. -- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
